    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm (MDS/MPN)&nbsp;NOS</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Eric Solary",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A combination of cytopenia(s) and proliferative feature(s)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bone marrow cytology:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A combination of cell dysplasia and proliferative features </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{22195406; 18480833; 15217205}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Molecular analyses of blood or bone marrow:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A combination of mutations seen in proliferative and dysplastic myeloid malignancies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 60.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.3pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">To be excluded:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Therapy-related myeloid neoplasms</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Disease-defining gene fusions such as <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> or rearrangement of <em>PDGFRA</em>, <em>PDGFRB</em>, <em>JAK2</em>, or <em>FGFR1</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Biallelic <em>TP53</em> mutations</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other MDS/MPN entities, including chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia, MDS/MPN with neutrophilia, and MDS/MPN with <em>SF3B1</em> mutation and thrombocytosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 65.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 65.3pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Specific situation:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 1cm; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Some MDS cases evolve to MDS/MPN-NOS with acquisition of proliferative features </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{19692701}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">. If the proliferative feature is persistent, these cases should be considered MDS/MPN-NOS, pending careful evaluation to ensure that proliferation is not reactive to growth factor administration, other previous or concurrent therapy, or a pathological situation (evaluation for the presence of a newly acquired mutation associated with proliferative features is encouraged).</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">MDS, myelodysplastic neoplasm.</span></p>",
